  "text_md": "On July 17th a public meeting was held to discuss the possibility of creating a Business Improvement District (BID) for Downtown Surfside. Redevelopment Management Associates (RMA) presented information on how BIDs work and described possible BID programs for Downtown Surfside. Similar to a Homeowners Association, but for commercial properties, a BID formalizes a process for property and business owners to work together to improve a commercial district.\nDesigned by the ﬁ rms of Stantac and Rosenberg Gradner, the Harding Avenue Streetscape plan will transform the downtown area with Medjool palms, colorful tropical shrubs and pocket parks with benches, pavers and street crossings.\n## Isaac Bashevis Singer Street Sign Unveiled\n- • Yogurt Spot – 9519 Harding\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile18.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile23.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile29.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile30.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile8.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile19.png>)\n### Ike’s Diner Now Open on Harding\nThe plans for the Harding Avenue Streetscape are now being reviewed by the Florida Department of Transportation, since Harding Avenue is a state-owned street. The Town is planning to start the project as soon as it is approved by the Florida DOT.\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile27.png>)\nIsaac Bashevis Singer, a 1978 winner of the Nobel Prize for literature and a leading ﬁ gure in Yiddish literature, was a resident of the Town in the 1980s. Now the Surfside street named in his honor has new, more prominent signage. A brief ceremony attended by residents and Town o ﬃ cials marked the unveiling of the signs on 95th Street. In addition to the Nobel prize, Singer also won two National Book Awards for his novels and short story collections. He died on July 24, 1991.\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile35.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile16.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile14.png>)\nBusiness Improvement District in Planning\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile24.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile17.png>)\n# ON HARDING AVE Isaac Bashevis Singer Street Sign Unveiled\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile34.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile5.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile25.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n![](<eac8e314c175b009ea2074f1bbef6922ca9d736b_page_1_images/imageFile13.png>)\nJoining the list of popular culinary establishments in the downtown district is Ike’s Diner, located at 9476 Harding Avenue. The Diner was created by a partnership between long-time restaurateur Samir Elnomany and Kosher Chef Yossi Horowitz. The diner serves breakfast all day, pastas, salads, pizzas, ﬁ sh, sandwiches, ice cream by the scoop and delicious iced coﬀ ees. Ike’s Diner is serving from 7:30 a.m. – 11 p.m. every day except Saturday. Home deliveries are available. For more information, call (305) 397-8559.",
